option_settings:
  "aws:elasticbeanstalk:container:python":
    WSGIPath: app:application
Your structure should end up like:

mlproject/
├── .ebextensions/
│   └── python.config
├── artifacts/
├── src/
├── templates/
├── app.py
└── requirements.txt
Two gotchas:

Windows Explorer refuses to create folders starting with a dot through the normal right-click menu. Use the terminal mkdir command above, or type the name as .ebextensions. (with a trailing dot) and Windows will strip it.
Make sure it's not nested inside another folder. .ebextensions must be at the top level of what gets zipped and deployed, or EB ignores it.
Then push:

git add .ebextensions
git commit -m "Add EB WSGI config"
git push origin main
Once CodePipeline finishes, reload the Beanstalk URL. Tell me what shows up.


